PIMID: run an x86_64 guest under -R (reserved_va) without the legacy vsyscall page

PIMID launches the guest with "-B 0 -R 0x8000000000": QEMU reserves the guest
address space at guest_base 0 before the program is loaded and places every
guest mapping in it with its own allocator. Without -R, QEMU 10 and later hand
a non-fixed guest mmap straight to the host kernel, so the guest's program,
stack and heap land among QEMU's and the plugin's own mappings, wherever the
host threads' allocations of the moment leave room; the simulated addresses
then depend on the host process.

QEMU refuses -R for an x86_64 guest ("Cannot allocate vsyscall page"): the
legacy vsyscall page sits at 0xffffffffff600000, outside any reservation.
With this patch the guest runs without that page under -R, as on a host
booted with vsyscall=none. glibc calls the time functions through the vDSO,
which QEMU provides; only binaries built against a glibc older than 2.14
(2011) called into the vsyscall page. Without -R nothing changes.

Applies to QEMU v11.1.2 (PIMID (1.12.62)). Apply inside external/qemu, after 0001:
    git apply ../qemu-patches/0002-x86_64-linux-user-reserved-va-without-vsyscall-page.patch

diff --git a/linux-user/x86_64/elfload.c b/linux-user/x86_64/elfload.c
index 49a6f61..97224ac 100644
--- a/linux-user/x86_64/elfload.c
+++ b/linux-user/x86_64/elfload.c
@@ -33,8 +33,13 @@ bool init_guest_commpage(void)
      */
     if (reserved_va != 0 &&
         TARGET_VSYSCALL_PAGE + TARGET_PAGE_SIZE - 1 > reserved_va) {
-        error_report("Cannot allocate vsyscall page");
-        exit(EXIT_FAILURE);
+        /*
+         * PIMID: with -R the guest runs without the legacy vsyscall page
+         * (as a host booted with vsyscall=none). glibc reaches the time
+         * calls through the vDSO, which QEMU provides; only binaries built
+         * against a pre-2011 glibc called into this page.
+         */
+        return true;
     }
     page_set_flags(TARGET_VSYSCALL_PAGE,
                    TARGET_VSYSCALL_PAGE | ~TARGET_PAGE_MASK,
